1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,785
Why does your dog sleep with its butt facing you?

2
00:00:02,835 --> 00:00:06,321
You'd think it's rude, especially if your dog is gassy.

3
00:00:06,371 --> 00:00:08,204
Vets say it may be the opposite.

4
00:00:08,254 --> 00:00:10,564
Turning its back to you may signal trust.

5
00:00:10,614 --> 00:00:14,869
In packs, dogs may sleep back-to-back so someone's always watching.

6
00:00:14,919 --> 00:00:20,115
A UK study found over 86% of dogs near people at night chose to be close.

7
00:00:20,165 --> 00:00:23,727
So that butt may be saying: I feel safe with you.

8
00:00:23,777 --> 00:00:28,432
Send this to someone whose dog gives them the butt every night.
